From 1a7e01459cb22bbecd4746559097c0102a9fb760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:18:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use the httprule parser for openapiv2 path templates

protoc-gen-openapiv2 had its own hand-written parser for the http.proto
path template syntax, duplicating the one in internal/httprule that
protoc-gen-grpc-gateway uses. Add httprule.SplitTemplate, which exposes
the top-level segments and verb of a parsed template, and build the
openapiv2 path parts from it so both generators split templates the same
way.

Path templates are already validated with httprule.Parse when the
descriptor registry is loaded, so only templates that the gateway accepts
reach the OpenAPI generator. Unit test inputs that httprule rejects (no
leading slash, trailing slash, ":" right after a "/") were updated or
removed accordingly. An explicit "{name=*}" is now treated like "{name}"
(as the gateway does) and no longer gets a redundant "[^/]+" pattern.

Fixes #2824
